e strong checksum; emit literal/copy tokens. http://oceanpark.com/webmuseum/rsync.html — That sliding-window match at arbitrary offsets is exactly the mechanism the offset-embed design needs.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Rolling-hash choice + window size at embed scale (~1–2 KB spans, not rsync's file blocks); strong-verify hash; minimum match run worth anchoring on.\n- Matcher output contract: token stream → span references + literal regions for the span-table schema (sibling follow-up under #6028).\n- Cost model: matcher CPU + reads vs embeddings saved, per source type (text vs prepend-heavy logs, where resync behaves worse).\n\n## Done looks like\n\nAn algorithm design with parameters, failure cases (reflow/re-wrap phantom diffs), and a worked run over Drew's 17–241 example.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=muse state=filed source=main-chat-2026-11-04-wave2 -->","closed_by":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"re